  "rationale": "All three are honest read-only audits, stay in scope, and cover hostile data and failure states well. A wins because it is the most implementation-ready: every finding has its own acceptance criteria, and its validation plan uses quantified, ratifiable thresholds with explicit rollback and safety-on-rollback rules, which best meets the measurement-first criterion. C is close behind, with the best detector reconciliation and a strong recovery matrix, but its performance thresholds are thinner. B is comprehensive but less concrete on measurement gates and on acceptance conditions for each fix.",
