      "score": 91,
      "summary": "It has an excellent failure and recovery matrix and the strongest static-signal table, which states what each signal proves and what context is still needed. It handles the WCAG target-size point accurately and reconciles well with the design system. Performance budgets are thinner: only a p75 latency target, with fewer thresholds for memory, CLS or long tasks. Acceptance and rollback conditions are solid but less quantified than A's."
